<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="024" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-11 client: default to version, override routes through link/graduate</title>
    <phase>2 Save flow</phase>
    <gate>023 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Save-path change with a named data-loss failure mode (NFR-08); modifies `.ts`/`.tsx` and touches the BFF dedup routing decision.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The override path carries the NFR-08 data-loss boundary: routing an editable document through the immutable suppress path collapses two distinct drafts into one record. Distinguishing link/graduate from suppress requires reading two dedup callers and judging which invariant applies.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>023,013</deps>
    <tags>frontend, fluent-ui, bff-api, office-addins, save-flow, dedup, data-integrity</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>When task 013 has resolved an existing `sprk_document` for the open Word document, the pane must DEFAULT to saving a new version of that record — sending `document.existingDocumentId` to the server hook task 023 made real. Offer an explicit "Save as new document" override, and route that override through the editable link/graduate dedup mode, never the immutable suppress path.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expertise in the Office add-in save flow (`useSaveFlow` / `SaveFlow`), Fluent UI v9 in a task pane, and the Spaarke content-identity layer — specifically the difference between the editable link/graduate mode and the immutable suppress mode. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>An identified document saves as a version by default (one `sprk_document` row, incremented SPE version). An explicit "Save as new document" override creates a new record and, when its bytes are byte-identical to an existing canonical, the new record carries `sprk_canonicaldocument` linkage (link/graduate) rather than being suppressed into the canonical. Integration tests assert both, including the `sprk_canonicaldocument` linkage on the override path.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec.md FR-11: when FR-01 resolves an existing `sprk_document`, DEFAULT to saving a new version of that record via `SaveRequest.ExistingDocumentId`; offer an explicit "Save as new document" override; the override path is routed through the editable link/graduate dedup mode.

      NFR-08 is the data-loss invariant this task exists to honor. A Word document is EDITABLE. The byte-identical editable save MUST use the LINK/GRADUATE mode, mirroring `Services/Compose/ComposeCreateOnSavePromoter.cs` `PromoteIfEphemeralAsync` (`:76`) — especially `GraduateLinkedCopyIfDivergedAsync` (`:116`), which severs `sprk_canonicaldocument` on divergence. It MUST NOT use the immutable suppress path in `Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs` (`ReconcileAsync` at `:78`), which is correct ONLY for email attachments and Assistant persist. Suppress-forever on an editable document collapses two distinct drafts into one record — that is data loss, not deduplication.

      Verified as-built (do not re-derive):
      - Attribute constants live on `ComposeService.cs`: `:89` `sprk_canonicalhash`, `:90` `sprk_canonicaldocument`.
      - `ContentDedupDetector` is at `Services/Documents/ContentDedupDetector.cs`: `ReconcileAsync:68` (suppress), `ResolveContentIdentityAsync:99` (pure), `FindCanonicalByHashAsync:127`. The add-in does NOT call it directly — `POST /api/office/save` already does. MUST NOT build a parallel check in the add-in.
      - Client save assembly is `useSaveFlow.ts`: `:760-767` picks contentType Email vs Document; `:844-859` is the Document branch (throws if no `documentContentBase64` at `:846-848`, forces `.docx` at `:852-853`); `:900-913` POSTs to `${apiBaseUrl}/api/office/save` via `authenticatedJsonFetch` with an `X-Idempotency-Key` header; `:540` is the job poll and `:719` the SSE stream.
      - `SaveFlow.tsx:895-903` is the footer action row (Cancel left, Save right) where the override affordance belongs.
      - The idempotency key at `OfficeService.cs:611-625` already includes `ExistingDocumentId` in its canonical string, so version and non-version saves of the same filename hash differently. The client key computation at `useSaveFlow.ts:888` must stay consistent with that.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useSaveFlow.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/SaveFlow.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/SaveView.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Office/OfficeDocumentPersistence.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeCreateOnSavePromoter.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Documents/ContentDedupDetector.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/__tests__/useSaveFlow.test.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="023" status="pending">FR-11 server — makes `ExistingDocumentId` / `IsNewVersion` / `VersionComment` real in `OfficeService.SaveAsync`. Without it the field this task sends is inert.</dependency>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">FR-01 client identity wiring — supplies the resolved `sprk_document` id that decides whether the default is version-save or create.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — NFR-08, the data-loss invariant: on the "Save as new document" override, a byte-identical editable document MUST be recorded via LINK/GRADUATE (a new row carrying `sprk_canonicaldocument` pointing at the canonical, graduating on divergence), mirroring `ComposeCreateOnSavePromoter.PromoteIfEphemeralAsync:76` and `GraduateLinkedCopyIfDivergedAsync:116`. It MUST NOT be routed through the immutable suppress path (`OfficeDocumentPersistence.ReconcileAsync:78`), which is correct only for email attachments and Assistant persist.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the add-in MUST NOT call `ContentDedupDetector` directly and MUST NOT implement a parallel content check client-side. `POST /api/office/save` already invokes the detector; the add-in rides it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the default when an identity is resolved is VERSION-SAVE. The override is explicit and user-initiated. MUST NOT make "create a new document" the default for an identified document, and MUST NOT silently version when the user chose the override.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — NFR-07: `sprk_graphitemid_uk` MUST NOT be relaxed. The override creates a genuinely new SPE item, so the key is satisfied naturally; do not work around it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the client idempotency key computed at `useSaveFlow.ts:888` MUST stay consistent with the server canonical string at `OfficeService.cs:611-625`, which already includes `ExistingDocumentId`. A version save and a fresh save of the same filename must not collide on the key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">SCOPE — the resolved document GUID sent as `existingDocumentId` MUST be canonicalized bare-lowercase via the shared `cleanGuid` before it leaves the client, and again at the server boundary.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE — for the version/override affordance: Fluent UI v9 semantic tokens only, no hex literals; the control and any state text honor the Office light/dark theme via `useOfficeTheme`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-050">SCOPE — if the override is presented as a modal rather than an inline control, it follows the canonical modal shell; per this project's Path C resolution, ADR-050 governs Spaarke-rendered modals. Prefer an inline control in the narrow pane; state the choice in the PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">SCOPE — for this add-in package only: per this project's Path A exception, keep the affordance a thin view under `shared/taskpane/`. MUST NOT import `@spaarke/ui-components`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — NFR-03: `Xrm.*` does not exist in an Office host. MUST NOT import any Xrm-bound component.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">SCOPE — this task changes save-path behavior, so it MUST add a data-mutation integration test asserting `sprk_canonicaldocument` linkage on the override path, plus contract coverage for the default version path. Cite `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md` — there is no concise copy in `.claude/adr/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — BFF publish size: measure the delta against a FRESH BUILD OF `origin/master`, never against the recorded baseline number (root CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4). Zip both with PowerShell `Compress-Archive` and report both absolute sizes, the delta, and the tool name.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the PR description MUST state the Placement Justification for any BFF-side change per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — run `/conflict-check` before opening this BFF PR. `spaarkeai-compose-r8` owns the link/graduate reference implementation this task mirrors, and `unified-access-control-r2` is live on the same hot path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — build commands for `src/client/office-addins` only: install with `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`; there is NO `build:prod` script — `npm run build` IS the production build.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Editable vs immutable dedup, Office save client flow, content identity</topic>
