    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="fluent-v9-host-visual-fit" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-host-visual-fit.md">Explicitly covers Office add-ins. The version/override affordance must sit in the narrow pane footer without crowding Cancel and Save.</pattern>
      <pattern name="endpoint-filters" location=".claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md">Any authorization on the target document stays on the save endpoint's filter, never in the client or the handler body.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/CLAUDE.md, spec.md FR-11 + NFR-07 + NFR-08, DEDUP-AND-SAVE-BACK-IDENTITY.md §3, and the knowledge files above. Output the mandatory rigor declaration (FULL) per root CLAUDE.md §8.</step>
    <step order="1">Read BOTH dedup callers side by side before writing code: `ComposeCreateOnSavePromoter.PromoteIfEphemeralAsync:76` (with `GraduateLinkedCopyIfDivergedAsync:116`) and `OfficeDocumentPersistence.ReconcileAsync` / `ContentDedupDetector.ReconcileAsync:68`. Write a one-paragraph statement of which mode this task's override path must take and why into projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/024-dedup-mode-decision.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Client: when task 013 resolved an identity, populate `document.existingDocumentId` (canonicalized via `cleanGuid`) and `document.isNewVersion` in the Document branch at `useSaveFlow.ts:844-859`, and carry a `versionComment` where the UI collects one.</step>
    <step order="3">Client: verify the idempotency key computation at `useSaveFlow.ts:888` still matches the server canonical string now that `existingDocumentId` participates. Add a unit test pinning that a version save and a non-version save of the same filename produce different keys.</step>
    <step order="4">Client UI: in the footer area of `SaveFlow.tsx`, show that the save will create a new version of the named existing record, plus an explicit "Save as new document" override. Announce the mode via `useAnnounce` (NFR-11).</step>
    <step order="5">Server: make the override path route through link/graduate. The override sends no `existingDocumentId`, so it lands on the create path — ensure that for an EDITABLE document the byte-identical outcome is a linked copy carrying `sprk_canonicaldocument`, not the suppress short-circuit that deletes the blob and returns the canonical id.</step>
    <step order="6">Add the data-mutation integration test: after an override save of byte-identical content, exactly one NEW `sprk_document` row exists and it carries `sprk_canonicaldocument` pointing at the canonical; after editing and re-saving, the link is severed (graduation).</step>
    <step order="7">Add contract coverage for the default version path: an identified document's save carries `existingDocumentId` and produces no second row.</step>
    <step order="8">Add client unit tests: default is version when identity resolved; default is create when not; the override forces create even when identity is resolved.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build`; run `dotnet build` and the Office contract + integration tests. All green.</step>
    <step order="10">Measure BFF publish size against a fresh `origin/master` build per the constraint above; record both absolute sizes, the delta, and the zip tool.</step>
    <step order="11">Run `/conflict-check`, then code-review + adr-check per task-execute Step 9.5.</step>
    <step order="12">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="13">Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the override path would route through the immutable suppress path rather than link/graduate, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — that is the NFR-08 data-loss failure mode, and no amount of downstream cleanup makes it acceptable.</trigger>
    <trigger>If achieving link/graduate from the Office save path requires modifying `ContentDedupDetector.cs` itself, STOP and escalate rather than editing the shared detector — `email-communication-intelligence-r2` shipped it and the immutable callers depend on its current semantics.</trigger>
    <trigger>If task 023 landed with different field semantics than this task assumes (for example `IsNewVersion` rather than `ExistingDocumentId` being the deciding field), STOP and reconcile with 023's implementation before sending anything, rather than sending both and hoping the server picks correctly.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Identified document defaults to version-save">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Spaarke-sourced Word document that resolves to an existing `sprk_document`, edit a sentence, and open the Save tab.</step>
        <step>Observe the save affordance before clicking anything, then Save.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The pane states that Save will create a new version of the named existing record; after saving, the record list shows ONE row for that document with an incremented version, not two rows.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Save as new document override">
      <steps>
        <step>On the same identified document, choose "Save as new document", pick a related record, and Save.</step>
        <step>Inspect the resulting `sprk_document` rows.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>A NEW `sprk_document` row is created; the original row is untouched; the new row carries `sprk_canonicaldocument` linkage when the bytes were identical.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Unidentified document has no version option">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a desktop-sourced document that resolves to no identity and view the Save tab.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>No version-save affordance appears; the pane presents a plain create save, and no `existingDocumentId` is sent.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark-mode check via the Office theme toggle">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the Office theme to Dark and reload the pane; view the version/override affordance in both its default and selected states.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colors resolve from Fluent v9 semantic tokens with legible contrast in dark mode; no hex literals; repeat in Light mode with the same result.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Mode change is announced (NFR-11)">
      <steps>
        <step>Using the keyboard only, toggle between version-save and "Save as new document".</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Each mode change is announced via `useAnnounce`; both modes are reachable and operable by keyboard.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build the BFF; run the Office contract and integration tests.</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Install with --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; typecheck, test, and build (build IS production here).</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
