  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a resolved document identity, when the user saves without choosing an override, then the request carries `document.existingDocumentId` (bare-lowercase canonicalized) and exactly one `sprk_document` row exists afterwards.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the "Save as new document" override on an identified document with byte-identical content, when the save completes, then a NEW `sprk_document` row exists AND it carries `sprk_canonicaldocument` linkage to the canonical — asserted by a data-mutation integration test that reads the column.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a linked copy created by the override, when its content is subsequently edited and re-saved, then `sprk_canonicaldocument` is severed (graduation), matching `GraduateLinkedCopyIfDivergedAsync` behavior.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the override path, when the save runs, then it does NOT take the immutable suppress branch: the uploaded blob is not deleted and the response does not redirect the user to a different canonical record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given NO resolved identity, when the user saves, then no `existingDocumentId` is sent and the save creates a new document exactly as before.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a version save and a non-version save of the same filename, when both idempotency keys are computed, then they differ — asserted by a client unit test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the add-in makes no direct call to `ContentDedupDetector` and contains no client-side content-hash comparison; verified by grep during code review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Office theme set to Dark, when the version/override affordance renders, then every color resolves from a Fluent v9 semantic token and no hex literal appears in the added styles.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`ContentDedupDetector.cs` is unmodified by this task; verified by `git diff --name-only`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run typecheck` is clean for the files this task touched; `npm test` and `npm run build` pass; `dotnet build` and the Office contract + integration tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size is measured against a fresh `origin/master` build with `Compress-Archive`, both absolute sizes and the delta are recorded, and the delta is under the +5 MB escalation threshold.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-11 (client half) + NFR-08 + Success Criterion 5; plan.md §4 Phase 2 task 024. DEDUP-AND-SAVE-BACK-IDENTITY.md §3 is the short version of the invariant: "if you stay on the item-identity, version-save path for Spaarke-sourced documents, you sidestep this entirely" — which is exactly why the DEFAULT is version-save and the override is the only path where the link/graduate decision arises.
  </notes>

